    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: bounded-prime-gaps-oq-03-oq-01-oq-04\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nD(k) is the diameter of admissible k-tuples: the smallest D such that there is an admissible k-tuple contained in {0,...,D}. For k=4, the target statement D(4)=8 has two parts: show {0,2,6,8} is admissible, and show no admissible 4-tuple has span less than 8.\n\n## Current Research State\n\nThe problem is active in OBSERVE phase on the fast path. No approaches have been tried yet, and the current focus is initial problem understanding and gathering context from problem.md.\n\n## Suggested First Steps\n\n1. Find the admissible tuple definition in the gallery proof.\n2. Prove {0,2,6,8} is admissible by checking the relevant prime obstructions.\n3. Prove every 4-tuple of span less than 8 fails admissibility.\n"
